abstract: >-
  COFY (Class-Owned Federated YOLO) is a federated object detector for sites that annotate different classes:
  only the site that owns a class updates that class's output parameters, unlabelled classes are masked in the
  loss and the server holds no data. It runs parallel (FedAvg), sequential (cyclic weight transfer) and
  concurrent asynchronous (FedAsync) training with a barrier-free calibration, a secured client-server
  implementation and ownership-aware robust aggregation. The release contains the code, the configurations,
  the frozen code and evaluation protocol of the article's ten-seed study, its run-level records and a
  one-machine demonstration.
keywords:
